-on-its-first-try-but-engine-problems-forced-it-to-return-to-the-planet-early-180989596/</link><description>两家航空航天公司正在竞相制造美国宇航局在将人类送回月球表面时使用的月球着陆器。但要到达我们的月球伙伴，航天器首先必须进入地球轨道</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:30:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacexs-giant-starship-rocket-reached-earth-orbit-on-its-first-try-but-engine-problems-forced-it-to-return-to-the-planet-early-180989596/</guid></item><item><title>一幅神秘的粉笔画在意大利私人收藏中被重新发现，被确认为爱德华·马奈失传已久的作品</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-enigmatic-chalk-drawing-rediscovered-in-a-private-italian-collection-has-been-identified-as-the-long-lost-work-of-edouard-manet-180989593/</link><description>一个年轻女孩的素描，采用了马奈 1860 年代生活研究特有的红色粉笔，被认为与该艺术家的几幅画有关。</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:55:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-enigmatic-chalk-drawing-rediscovered-in-a-private-italian-collection-has-been-identified-as-the-long-lost-work-of-edouard-manet-180989593/</guid></item><item><title>土星的卫星土卫二可能存在外星生命吗？地球微生物可以在其模拟环境中生存，提高其潜在的宜居性</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-saturns-moon-enceladus-host-alien-life-earth-microbes-can-live-in-its-simulated-environment-boosting-its-potential-habitability-180989589/</link><description>土卫二被冰覆盖，但该层可能隐藏着地下海洋。研究人员长期以来一直想知道咸水体是否具有适宜生命生存的条件，现在，一个研究小组表明，地球上喜热的生物体可以在那里繁衍生息</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:00:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-saturns-moon-enceladus-host-alien-life-earth-microbes-can-live-in-its-simulated-environment-boosting-its-potential-habitability-180989589/</guid></item><item><title>东北复活节期间，有人发现一只鲨鱼在新泽西州被洪水淹没的街道上游动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-shark-was-spotted-swimming-through-the-flooded-streets-of-new-jersey-during-the-noreaster-180989588/</link><description>该生物已被确认为光滑角鲨，这是一种在西大西洋发现的无害物种。它并不是唯一陷入风暴系统带来的混乱的动物</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-shark-was-spotted-swimming-through-the-flooded-streets-of-new-jersey-during-the-noreaster-180989588/</guid></item><item><title>英格兰备受喜爱的梧桐树在被破坏者砍倒三年后又显现出了生命的迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/englands-beloved-sycamore-gap-tree-is-showing-signs-of-life-three-years-after-vandals-chopped-it-down-180989591/</link><description>现在，位于英格兰北部哈德良长城附近的树桩底部周围正在长出许多绿叶芽。</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/englands-beloved-sycamore-gap-tree-is-showing-signs-of-life-three-years-after-vandals-chopped-it-down-180989591/</guid></item><item><title>当简·奥斯汀在巴斯的舞厅转一圈时，古罗马文物就藏在她的脚下。现在，考古学家终于找到了它们</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-jane-austen-took-a-turn-about-the-ballroom-in-bath-ancient-roman-artifacts-were-hiding-beneath-her-feet-now-archaeologists-have-finally-found-them-180989592/</link><description>最近在英格兰巴斯集会室进行的发掘发现了罗马时代的硬币、屋顶瓦片、陶器、玻璃器皿、沟渠网络和军用头盔的碎片</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-jane-austen-took-a-turn-about-the-ballroom-in-bath-ancient-roman-artifacts-were-hiding-beneath-her-feet-now-archaeologists-have-finally-found-them-180989592/</guid></item><item><title>核磁共振扫描可能会在大脑中出现蛛丝马迹七年前发现阿尔茨海默病的迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mri-scans-might-reveal-signs-of-alzheimers-disease-seven-years-before-a-telltale-marker-appears-in-the-brain-180989570/</link><description>并非所有研究人员都相信通过 MRI 检测到的大脑变化足以成为诊断工具。但这些发现可以帮助研究人员更好地了解驱动神经退行性疾病的机制</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:33:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mri-scans-might-reveal-signs-of-alzheimers-disease-seven-years-before-a-telltale-marker-appears-in-the-brain-180989570/</guid></item><item><title>在罗马最著名和最被忽视的别墅之一，由修女绘制的具有数百年历史的下流壁画重新出现</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-one-of-romes-most-famed-and-neglected-villas-centuries-old-risque-frescoes-painted-over-by-nuns-have-reappeared-180989585/</link><description>耗资 4000 万美元修复西尔维斯特里里瓦尔迪别墅近一年后，保护人员正在重新发现和复兴 16 世纪的艺术</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-one-of-romes-most-famed-and-neglected-villas-centuries-old-risque-frescoes-painted-over-by-nuns-have-reappeared-180989585/</guid></item><item><title>Anthropic 表示其人工智能发现了一种新的酶系统，类似于革命性的基因编辑工具 CRISPR</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/anthropic-says-its-ai-discovered-a-new-enzyme-system-that-resembles-the-revolutionary-gene-editing-tool-crispr-180989578/</link><description>该公司的专家不知道新发现的系统有什么作用，因此它在生物学中的潜在用途（如果有的话）仍不清楚。但这项工作标志着一项重大进步，因为人工智能主要是靠自己做出这一发现的</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:16:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/anthropic-says-its-ai-discovered-a-new-enzyme-system-that-resembles-the-revolutionary-gene-editing-tool-crispr-180989578/</guid></item><item><title>密尔沃基艺术博物馆刚刚将两件由被奴役的波特大卫·德雷克制作的陶瓷归还给他的后裔</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-milwaukee-art-museum-just-returned-two-ceramics-made-by-enslaved-potter-david-drake-to-his-descendants-180989586/</link><description>这两艘船是德雷克家族最近重新安置的两艘船，其中一艘是 1855 年签名的罐子，他们的使命是获取祖先的作品</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:07:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-milwaukee-art-museum-just-returned-two-ceramics-made-by-enslaved-potter-david-drake-to-his-descendants-180989586/</guid></item><item><title>两个头比一个好：科德角发现的稀有双头海龟幼体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-heads-are-better-than-one-rare-double-headed-turtle-hatchling-discovered-on-cape-cod-180989579/</link><description>9 月 17 日，这种微小的小菜斑龟被带到野生动物中心。当时，这种生物的重量约为 5 分钱。</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:33:21 GMT